    "33": {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "##### Run duration\nThe table ranks locations by change rather than absolute duration. This helps distinguish one degrading region from an application that became slower everywhere. The trend shows the raw trajectory for each location."
    },
    "40": {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "### 1 · Overall health\nThe fastest way to check whether the test estate has a broad problem. Aggregate values can hide individual failures, so healthy results here don't rule out an issue with a specific test."
    },
    "41": {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "### 2 · Tests, steps and failures\nAvailability and run duration by test, failure trends by error code, and step-level details for multi-step journeys."
    },
    "42": {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "### 3 · Locations\nAvailability and run duration by runner location. Use this section to distinguish a runner or regional issue from an application-wide degradation."
    },
    "43": {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "### 4 · Individual runs\nIndividual executions behind an anomaly, sorted with failures first. Use error codes, messages, and locations to investigate a specific incident."
    },
